# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ONE RULE. Everything this project must never publish lives in _private/.
#
# This file used to be a DENYLIST - 59 rules naming ~30 scattered locations, to
# protect a publish set of 35 files. A denylist fails OPEN: anything NEW is
# publishable until somebody remembers to add a rule. That was not remembered
# three times:
#
#   2026-09-06  _scripts/redgold/     31 customer logos   caught by hand
#   2026-09-08  _scripts/_not-logos/  47 files, 27.7 MB   went public
#   2026-09-08  HANDOFF.md            internal notes      went public
#
# Every one was a NEW name no existing rule described. A 60th rule would have
# fixed the last incident and not the next one. One default-denied directory
# fixes every future one, because a file created inside it is covered the
# moment it exists and nobody has to predict its name.
#
# So: if it must never be published, PUT IT IN _private/. Do not add a rule
# here. Adding rules here is what stopped working.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
_private/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The two exceptions, and they are exceptions for a specific reason.
#
# These are fixed, well-known filenames that never change - the .env case,
# where a denylist genuinely works. CLAUDE.md must sit at the project root to
# be auto-loaded by Claude Code and to satisfy the ICM convention, so it cannot
# live in _private/. The directory rule exists for material whose names churn.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CLAUDE.md
CONTEXT.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build products and caches. Regenerated, never authored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
.venv-*/
dist/
build/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.lineart_cache/
app/.work/
app/.chrome-profile/
app/T-Tracer
app/T-Tracer.cmd
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Safety net, kept deliberately. Tyler drops customer images in the project
# root by habit (twice on 2026-09-07), and a customer logo reaching the public
# repo is the one unrecoverable mistake this project can make. The pre-push
# hook is the real guard now - see .githooks/pre-push - but belt and braces.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.webp
/*.bmp

# T-Tracer.png is the README hero image and IS published; the /*.png safety
# net above would otherwise catch it on a re-add.
!/T-Tracer.png
